  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Lofted balls in a square and lofted tennis",
  "description": "Split the players into four groups standing at the corners of a big rectangle – the long sides run along the rink, the short sides across it. Keep spare balls with B and D.\n\nA plays a long lofted ball to B. B brings it down, gets control and passes along the ice to C. C lofts it long back to D, who brings it down and passes along the ice to A. After their turn, A and D swap groups, and so do B and C.\n\nVariant – lofted tennis: players stand in pairs 8–10 metres apart. A lofts the ball to B, who plays it straight back in the air or after one bounce. Swap roles when the coach says so. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The lofted ball: blade under the ball and a follow-through upwards – no chopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Bring the ball down with a soft stick or the body and get it onto the ice quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Get into the line of the ball early and move your feet, not just the stick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The ice pass after the control must be as accurate as the lofted ball."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
